# In a loop, `x instanceof Dog` is decided from the shapes of the class hierarchy of Dog, after one guard on the prototype links of every class in it.
# Out of the compiler's sight, the prototype of Cat.prototype is set to Dog.prototype, so cats are dogs.
# Fault injection, testing=SkipHierarchyGuards: the guard on the prototype links of the class hierarchy is not built, so the shape of a Cat still gives false.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) each result derived from shapes is checked against a walk of the prototype chain that gives up at a trap and runs no code.
# If they disagree, the process crashes.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 2 4
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(WRONG): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipHierarchyGuards
# WRONG: 2 2
# WRONG-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipHierarchyGuards,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed
# HELD-NEXT: in the result of an operation
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
